From f0a6357469fd593f1778e37f683bc0da3020c8ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:53:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: spell the RegionErrorHandler cache guard with its
 short name and state the NotLeader exception (#680)

The invalidation guard of RegionErrorHandler::check() tested the optional
cache against the fully-qualified RegionCacheInterface name although the
file imports it. The check is the null check of ?RegionCacheInterface
$cache (a region id without a cache must not call invalidate() on null),
and Rector's FlipTypeControlToUseExclusiveTypeRector turns $cache !== null
back into an instanceof, so it keeps that form with the short name.

The first paragraph of the docblock said a cache and a region id always
invalidate the region; it now names the NotLeader exception the docblock
describes further down.

Closes #680
---
 CHANGELOG.md                             |  4 ++++
 docs/helpers/faq.md                      | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 src/Client/Region/RegionErrorHandler.php |  8 +++++---
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index af36e5a..7dfed57 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@ policy now classifies as internal.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `RegionErrorHandler::check()` spells its cache guard with the imported short name (`$cache instanceof RegionCacheInterface`) instead of the fully-qualified interface name, and the first paragraph of its docblock now states the NotLeader exception that the same docblock describes further down: a NotLeader error at a site owned by a `RetryExecutor` is left cached even when a cache and a region id are passed. The guard is not always true — it is the null check of the optional `$cache` (`testRegionErrorWithoutCacheDoesNotThrowFromInvalidation()` pins it) — and it stays an `instanceof` because Rector's `FlipTypeControlToUseExclusiveTypeRector` rewrites `$cache !== null` back into it. No behaviour change. (#680)
+
 ## [v0.9.0] - 2026-10-21
 
 ### Added
diff --git a/docs/helpers/faq.md b/docs/helpers/faq.md
index b12205f..7ff5b43 100644
--- a/docs/helpers/faq.md
+++ b/docs/helpers/faq.md
@@ -2497,4 +2497,17 @@ Say so where the behaviour is documented (`docs/configuration.md`), and say
 what the user has to do: configure the logger's level and handlers before
 the client is built, and build a new client after changing them. A
 limitation that is only described in the commit message is a limitation
-that the next integrator re-discovers the hard way.
\ No newline at end of file
+that the next integrator re-discovers the hard way.
+
+## An `instanceof` of a parameter's own nullable type is its null check, and Rector keeps it that way
+
+`RegionErrorHandler::check()` takes `?RegionCacheInterface $cache` and guards the
+invalidation with `$cache instanceof RegionCacheInterface`. That is not an
+always-true check: it is the only thing that stops `$cache->invalidate()` from
+being called on `null` when a caller passes a region id without a cache
+(`testRegionErrorWithoutCacheDoesNotThrowFromInvalidation()` pins it). Do not
+rewrite it as `$cache !== null` either: Rector's
+`FlipTypeControlToUseExclusiveTypeRector` flips a null comparison of an
+object-typed variable into an `instanceof`, so `bin/lint.sh` fails until the
+`instanceof` is back. Spell it with the imported short name — Rector writes the
+fully-qualified name when it does the flip itself. (#680)
diff --git a/src/Client/Region/RegionErrorHandler.php b/src/Client/Region/RegionErrorHandler.php
index 230a557..b6cdabc 100644
--- a/src/Client/Region/RegionErrorHandler.php
+++ b/src/Client/Region/RegionErrorHandler.php
@@ -33,8 +33,10 @@ final class RegionErrorHandler
      * instead of a silently accepted response.
      *
      * When a $cache and $regionId are provided, the region is invalidated
-     * from the cache before the exception is thrown. This is the consistent
-     * behaviour expected by Transaction and LockResolver callers.
+     * from the cache before the exception is thrown — except for a NotLeader
+     * error at a site owned by a RetryExecutor, which is left cached (see
+     * below). This is the consistent behaviour expected by Transaction and
+     * LockResolver callers.
      *
      * NotLeader ownership depends on where check() runs:
      *
@@ -68,7 +70,7 @@ final class RegionErrorHandler
                 $isNotLeader = $regionError->getNotLeader() !== null;
                 if (
                     (!$isNotLeader || !$notLeaderOwnedByRetryExecutor)
-                    && $cache instanceof \CrazyGoat\TiKV\Client\Cache\RegionCacheInterface
+                    && $cache instanceof RegionCacheInterface
                     && $regionId !== null
                 ) {
                     $cache->invalidate($regionId, $isNotLeader ? 'not_leader' : 'region_error');
